    "created_at": "2020-04-20T20:45:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-20T20:45:50Z",
    "body": "OK so, if a custom element is both form-associated and focusable (because it has `tabindex` or otherwise), it seems reasonable to include it in \"interactive content\" and \"labelable\" categories, so it works right with `<label>`.\r\n\r\nRight now all form-associated custom elements are \"labelable\" per spec afaict. Since there are native form-associated elements that aren't labelable, maybe they shouldn't be labelable when they aren't focusable (e.g. for `custom-output` or `custom-fieldset`).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
